  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "In the year she turned nineteen, Anna Kovac took the sleeper from Vienna to Venice, and the carriages smelled of diesel and oranges. This spring she made the trip again, in a refitted cabin with a reading lamp, a folding desk and a door that locks. Nothing about the route had changed, except that people had once decided to give it up.",
