  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Austria's national railway was the first to bet on a revival. It bought used carriages from a bankrupt competitor, rebuilt them, and filled them within a season. Sweden, France and Italy followed, each wary of repeating the mistakes of the past. The cabins must be quiet, the timetable must make sense, and the price must not feel like a punishment.",
