  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "A sleeper berth costs several times what a seat does to run. A carriage that carries sixty people by day carries only twenty-four at night, and it spends the small hours standing in sidings while crews rest. Operators say a typical overnight train needs a public subsidy of about forty euros for each passenger it carries, roughly the price of the ticket itself.",
